# Audience-based Individual Game. These scripts are generated from Admin when
# Rooney's live recording is ready; the customer only sees the audio controls.
TEXTS.update({
    "audience_opening": "Welcome. We are going to build practical fundraising ideas around your organization's goal. Start with the people who have the strongest reason to care, then think through why they would give, where to find them, what would attract them, what to ask them to fund and the process that can move them from first contact to support.",
    "audience_individuals_audience": "Start with individual donors. Think about the type or group of people with the strongest personal, community or values-based reason to help your organization reach this goal. Be specific enough that the organization could recognize and find them.",
    "audience_individuals_reason": "Now explain the reason. What connects these people to the mission, the people served or the outcome this fundraising goal will create?",
    "audience_individuals_where": "Think about where these people already gather, work, learn, worship, network or spend their attention. Name the places and channels where the organization can consistently find them.",
    "audience_individuals_attraction": "Before asking for money, give people a reason to engage. Think about useful information, an experience, an event, a story or another valuable opportunity that would earn their attention and contact details.",
    "audience_individuals_funding_ask": "Make the future ask concrete. What part of the goal should these individuals help fund, and what amount or giving range would make sense for each person?",
    "audience_individuals_process": "Now describe the relationship journey. Explain the practical steps from first discovery, to interest and trust, to the ask, follow-up and continued stewardship.",
    "audience_businesses_gate": "If you know a type of business with a strong reason to support this goal, continue. If no business audience comes to mind, it is all right to move forward without inventing one.",
    "audience_businesses_audience": "Which types of businesses have the strongest reason to sponsor the organization, its programs or the people it serves? Be specific about the business profile.",
    "audience_businesses_reason": "Explain why those businesses would care. Consider their customers, employees, location, values, community commitments or commercial connection to the people and outcome involved.",
    "audience_businesses_where": "Where can the organization find these businesses and the people who make sponsorship or community-investment decisions?",
    "audience_businesses_attraction": "What partnership value, credible evidence, useful opportunity or shared community outcome would earn a conversation with these businesses?",
    "audience_businesses_funding_ask": "What should these businesses sponsor or fund, and what contribution or sponsorship amount should the organization ask for?",
    "audience_businesses_process": "Describe the practical process from identifying the right business and decision maker, through introduction and relationship building, to the proposal, follow-up and partnership stewardship.",
    "audience_grantors_gate": "If you know a type of grantor that aligns with this mission or goal, continue. If none comes to mind, move forward without guessing.",
    "audience_grantors_audience": "Which type of foundation, public funder or other grantmaker has the strongest reason to fund this mission, program or outcome?",
    "audience_grantors_reason": "Explain why the organization's work aligns with that grantor type's priorities, population, geography or intended outcomes.",
    "audience_grantors_where": "Where can the organization identify these grantors, their priorities, application opportunities and the people responsible for the funding program?",
    "audience_grantors_attraction": "Grant fundraising begins before the application. Explain how the organization can demonstrate relevance, evidence, credibility and readiness to strengthen the relationship and the application case.",
    "audience_grantors_funding_ask": "What should the organization ask these grantors to fund, and what request amount or range fits the goal and intended work?",
    "audience_grantors_process": "Describe the full grant process, including research, qualification, relationship building, case development, application, follow-up, reporting and stewardship.",
    "audience_involvement": "Finally, think about where you would be comfortable and genuinely useful. Describe the introductions, research, outreach, relationship building, asking, follow-up or other fundraising support you would be willing to provide.",
})

